Abstract classes
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/kotlin/kotlin-abstract-class
https://www.programiz.com/kotlin-programming/abstract-class
https://kotlinlang.org/docs/classes.html#abstract-classes

you cannot create an object from it directly
you can only inherit from that class

abstract class is there to add general ideas, not specific params that need to be used
 Abstract classes are always open. You do not need to explicitly use open keyword to inherit subclasses from them.



Interfaces
https://kotlinlang.org/docs/interfaces.html
https://www.programiz.com/kotlin-programming/interfaces
https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/kotlin/kotlin-interfaces/
https://www.baeldung.com/kotlin/interfaces

set of functions (or parameters) that a class need to implement
Kotlin interfaces are similar to abstract classes. However, interfaces cannot store state whereas abstract classes can.

Meaning, interface may have property but it needs to be abstract or has to provide accessor implementations. Whereas, it's not mandatory for property of an abstract class to be abstract.


